NAME
    ls - list directory entries

SYNOPSIS
    ls [-a] [-l] [path]

DESCRIPTION
    Lists a real directory's entries (default: current directory), or a
    single file listed as itself. One entry per line, no multi-column
    terminal layout. -a includes dotfiles; -l shows a simplified type/size/
    modified-time/name line (no permission bits/owner/group - this project
    has no such concept to show). Walled to the project's own directory
    tree - see 'cd'.

EXAMPLES
    ls
    ls -la EmuSen
